# test2c.ledc — feature-coverage test, part C of 3 (LED colour/brightness mods + antiphase).
# Self-contained: at t=0 all 8 audio channels (ch1..ch8) get a calm sine/triangle bed and the
# LED masks are set up. Channels PERSIST once set. Strict 10 s steps (0,10000,20000,...), then a
# ~5 s fade of all 8 audio channels + LED masks. EXACTLY 8 audio channels live at once.
# Audio vols moderate (~40..50). S speech lines are browser-only (don't count toward device cap).
# The audio bed here is deliberately simple — this file exercises the LED feature set.
# DIRECT/mono board ignores colour (brightness + flicker still show); NeoPixel shows colour.
# Play via the web app.
#
# Coverage in this file (LED):
#   brightness ramp > (linear) and * (quadratic); brightness periodic mod; colour ramp (RGB
#   linear); colour periodic mod (~ sine incl. freq-0 DC chromatic swap ~255:0:25 / ~0:255:25);
#   antiphase pair (phase 0 vs 180, two masks) -> luminance-flat "invisible" flicker; DIM 20 Hz
#   strobe-safe band (bright <=20%); every mod glyph: ~ sine, ^ triangle, / sawup, \ sawdn, _ square.
#
# Fields —  LED: <time> <freq> <duty> <bright> <R> <G> <B> <mask> [env phase attack jitter]
#   glyphs: >lin *quad ~sine ^tri /sawup \sawdn _square ; '-' = keep current

# ===== 0 s — STEP one — setup: 8-channel calm sine/triangle audio bed
#            LED: steady white (freq 0), mask 1 — baseline before the mod showcase
S 0 default 20 "this is a test"
S 2000 default 20 "one"
0 0 50 45 255 255 255 1
A 0 196 -50 50 0 1 0 0          # ch1 sine, panned left
A 0 220 -30 50 0 2 0 0          # ch2 sine
A 0 247 -10 50 0 3 0 0          # ch3 sine
A 0 262  10 50 0 4 0 2          # ch4 triangle
A 0 294  30 50 0 5 0 0          # ch5 sine
A 0 330  50 50 0 6 0 2          # ch6 triangle
A 0 349  0  45 0 7 0 0          # ch7 sine
A 0 392  0  45 0 8 0 0          # ch8 sine

# ===== 10 s — STEP two — LED brightness ramps: > (linear) and * (quadratic) on two masks
#            (audio bed unchanged)
S 10000 default 20 "this is a test"
S 12000 default 20 "two"
10000 0 50 >10 0 128 255 1      # mask1: brightness linear ramp 10 -> 60 (blue)
10000 0 50 *10 255 128 0 2      # mask2: brightness quadratic ramp 10 -> 70 (orange)
20000 0 50 60 0 128 255 1       # mask1 brightness-ramp target
20000 0 50 70 255 128 0 2       # mask2 brightness-ramp target

# ===== 20 s — STEP three — LED colour ramp (RGB linear >) + brightness periodic mod (^ triangle)
S 20000 default 20 "this is a test"
S 22000 default 20 "three"
20000 4 50 40 >0 >255 >0 4      # mask4: 4 Hz, colour linear ramp green -> orange (RGB ramps)
20000 0 50 ^10:60:2000 128 0 255 8  # mask8: brightness triangle mod 10<->60 / 2 s (purple)
30000 4 50 40 255 120 0 4       # mask4 colour-ramp target (green -> orange completes)

# ===== 30 s — STEP four — LED colour periodic mod (~ sine) incl. freq-0 DC chromatic swap
S 30000 default 20 "this is a test"
S 32000 default 20 "four"
30000 0 50 45 ~255:0:25 ~0:255:25 0 1   # mask1: freq-0 DC red<->green chromatic swap @ ~40 Hz
30000 0 50 45 ~255:0:2000 0 ~0:255:2000 2   # mask2: slow red<->blue sine colour mod (2 s)

# ===== 40 s — STEP five — LED antiphase invisible-flicker pair (phase 0 vs 180, two masks)
#            + DIM 20 Hz strobe-safe band (bright <=20%) + remaining glyphs on brightness
S 40000 default 20 "this is a test"
S 42000 default 20 "five"
40000 8 50 40 255 160 0 4 1 0      # mask4: 8 Hz, sine env, phase 0   (amber)  — antiphase pair A
40000 8 50 40 0 100 255 8 1 180    # mask8: 8 Hz, sine env, phase 180 (blue)   — antiphase pair B
40000 20 50 18 0 255 255 1 0       # mask1: 20 Hz DIM (bright 18 <=20% strobe-safe, cyan)
40000 0 50 /5:60:2000 255 0 255 2  # mask2: brightness sawup mod (/ glyph, magenta)

# ===== 50 s — STEP six — remaining glyphs: \ sawdn + _ square on brightness (two masks)
#            (antiphase pair on mask4/mask8 + audio bed persist from earlier steps)
S 50000 default 20 "this is a test"
S 52000 default 20 "six"
50000 0 50 \10:60:2000 0 255 0 1   # mask1: brightness sawdn mod (\ glyph, green)
50000 0 50 _10:60:1000 255 0 0 2   # mask2: brightness square mod (_ glyph, red)

# ===== 60 s — STEP seven — closing: ~5 s linear fade-out of all 8 audio channels + LED masks
S 60000 default 20 "this is a test"
S 62000 default 20 "seven"
60000 0 50 >40 0 255 0 1        # mask1 brightness ramp -> 0
60000 0 50 >40 255 0 0 2        # mask2 brightness ramp -> 0
60000 0 50 >40 255 120 0 4      # mask4 brightness ramp -> 0
60000 0 50 >40 0 100 255 8      # mask8 brightness ramp -> 0
A 60000 - - >50 - 1            # hold vols then ramp to 0 (targets at 65 s)
A 60000 - - >50 - 2
A 60000 - - >50 - 3
A 60000 - - >50 - 4
A 60000 - - >50 - 5
A 60000 - - >50 - 6
A 60000 - - >45 - 7
A 60000 - - >45 - 8
A 65000 - - 0 - 1             # fade-out targets (~5 s): all 8 channels to zero
A 65000 - - 0 - 2
A 65000 - - 0 - 3
A 65000 - - 0 - 4
A 65000 - - 0 - 5
A 65000 - - 0 - 6
A 65000 - - 0 - 7
A 65000 - - 0 - 8
65000 0 50 0 0 255 0 1         # mask1 brightness reaches 0
65000 0 50 0 255 0 0 2         # mask2 brightness reaches 0
65000 0 50 0 255 120 0 4       # mask4 brightness reaches 0
65000 0 50 0 0 100 255 8       # mask8 brightness reaches 0
